hi I am Missy Franklin I am an Olympic  swimmer and my favorite movie is Bend It  Like Beckham I would say Bend It Like  Beckham influences means an Olympic  athlete just because it was so inspiring  watching Jess as as an athlete as a  woman and kind of having to fight so  much to really truly do what she loves  it's just something so inspiring about  that that really motivated me as an  Olympian my body tells me know quite a  bit I put it through a very vigorous  routine every single day work out about  four to five hours a day and swim 12 to  13 thousand meters a day and there's  many times in my body says no I don't  want to do this this is tiring and I'm  exhausted and and I just want to rest  and it's those moments where you need to  tell your body yes that it can do this  and that you are capable of achieving  your goals honestly I think my favorite  scene from Bend It Like Beckham is the  first time she puts on shorts and she  has the burn on her leg and she's really  nervous about going out onto the field  and showing her burn and see Jess like  get up from that and go onto the field  and sort of show herself to people in a  way she's never let people see her  before and overcoming this thing that  used to shame her that now it doesn't  matter because she's playing football  and that's all that she really cares  about that was a really inspiring moment  for me watching Bend It Like Beckham and  and seeing Jess's situation it really  gave me an appreciation for mine I had  never really known anything different  than having a supportive family that was  a hundred percent behind me whatever my  decision was and so to watch Jess in her  situation and watch her parents really  struggle with the fact that she wanted  to be a football player and especially  you know running around in short shorts  and like having her mom be upset about  that and being against kind of what they  believed in I had never experienced  anything like that and it's something  that I never want to take for granted I  live my dream every single day being  able to go to the Olympics has always  been a dream for me but also just doing  what I love every day is a dream come  true for me I love that I get up and go  to practice and see my teammates and I  get to work so hard and that's why I'm  so grateful to have that opportunity and  I know not everyone gets those same  opportunities and that  I want to make the most of mine I am  Missy Franklin and I love movies
 

